= Chiang Kai-shek Succeeds Xu Chongzhi

Hu Hanmin's exile had sent shockwaves throughout the party, but this has become it's greatest consequence.

Also suspected in Liao Zhongkai's murder is General Xu Chongzhi, the commander of the National Revolutionary Army. Because of this, Xu Chongzhi was removed from his position.

Since the Right faction's other leaders were demoted, and the Communists had banded with Wang Jingwei after Liao Zhongkai's death, Chiang Kai-shek has suddenly become the second-most influential man in the party.

By convincing the Right Faction and many of the party's centrists, as well as Chiang Kai-shek's control over the NRA, he is now the final contender against Wang Jingwei.

The KMT is now approaching an impasse, and it will take a sudden event to take down one of the other candidates. Who will win this now?
